diff --git a/features/stable-rows.feature b/features/stable-rows.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c5a4e6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/stable-rows.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+Feature: Stable rows across state changes
+  As a person interacting with the todo list
+  I want a todo's row to stay in place when its state changes
+  So that the row I just clicked is not thrown away and rebuilt
+
+  Rule: A state change updates the existing row in place, keyed by todo
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo's toggle updates its row in place
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And I note the row element of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And I note the row element of the todo "Walk the dog"
+    When I check the toggle of the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the same row element noted before
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is in the same row element noted before
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is marked as complete
+
+  Scenario: Marking all complete updates every existing row in place
+    Given the todo app has the todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+    And I note the row element of the todo "Buy milk"
+    And I note the row element of the todo "Walk the dog"
+    When I check the mark-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the same row element noted before
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is in the same row element noted before
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is marked as complete
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is marked as complete
